   digest: A decaying planar rotation is uniformly bounded but has no contractive positive weight. -/

/- Source: Madou–Remizov–Vafadar (eds.), "Open problems in one-parameter
   operator semigroups theory", arXiv:2410.00416v2, §6, Problem 22,
   with the setting of Problem 21 and inequality (3).
   The measure space is Fin n with counting measure, V = ℂⁿ, and
   a(u,v) = ∑ i, (A *ᵥ u) i * star (v i). All vectors lie in L² ∩ L∞.
   Positive weights on a finite space and their reciprocals are bounded.
   Finite-dimensional sectorial forms are densely defined and closed.
   admission_basis: open-problem-resolution (#15711; Refuted)
   escape_witness: none
   Direct frozen dependencies: none (pinned Mathlib only).
   Reuse: Complex.liftAux, Complex.liftAux_apply, NormedSpace.map_exp,
     Complex.exp_eq_exp_ℂ, Complex.exp_re, Complex.exp_im,
     Real.exp_le_one_iff, Real.abs_cos_le_one, Real.abs_sin_le_one,
     norm_sum_le, norm_le_pi_norm, pi_norm_le_iff_of_nonneg,
     LinearMap.continuous_of_finiteDimensional,
     eventually_nhdsWithin_sign_eq_of_deriv_pos, nhdsGT_neBot, Complex.re_le_norm.
   Definitions:
     supNorm: proof_shape definition; consumers=claim, bounded, no_weight
     IsSectorialMatrix: proof_shape definition; consumers=claim, sectorial
     semigroup: proof_shape definition; consumers=claim, semigroup_formula,
       entry_bound, bounded, action, no_weight
     claim: proof_shape definition; consumer=result
     A: proof_shape definition; consumers=sectorial, semigroup_formula,
       entry_bound, bounded, action, no_weight, result
     J: proof_shape definition; consumers=J_sq, φ, φ_apply
